    remoteproc: qcom_wcnss: Request PD regulators on Pronto v1/v2
    
    The v3 guard compares possible power domains with the number of non-PD
    regulators. Pronto v1/v2 also have two possible domains and one non-PD
    regulator, so the guard selects only the first table entry, vddcx.
    It omits MX/PX for one attached domain and PX for two attached domains.
    Legacy DTs without domains also lose MX/PX.
    
    Identify tables without PD regulators using num_pd_vregs directly,
    retaining the v3 bounds protection and correct v1/v2 table selection.
    
    The source-extracted host fixture reproduces six wrong selections among
    eight platform/domain cases before this change. Error injection covers
    allocation and regulator-get failures. Real regulator hardware is untested.
    
    Refresh the existing implementation from 61c60256c94a, originally by
    Timothy Schmidt with Claude Opus 5.5 assistance. This current-base refresh
    and qualification used OpenAI Codex; human review and DCO are pending.
    
    Fixes: 3dbc90b9c22e ("remoteproc: qcom_wcnss: Fix handling the lack of PD regulators in v3")
    
    Assisted-by: LLM

